    "durationMs": 80132,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified:\n\n- **`server.js`** — Express 5 app with all routes: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL unchanged), `GET /links/:code`, `GET /r/:code` (302 + atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` click increment), `GET /links` (creation order + total). Error mapping: 409 duplicate code (caught from Postgres unique violation, race-safe), 422 for malformed JSON / missing-invalid URL / invalid code, 404 unknown codes. Generated codes are 8 random chars from the allowed alphabet with collision retry.\n- **Persistence** — Knex 3 + `pg`, reading `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded creds), with a `links` migration; `sh start.sh` applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **Tested** — all 14 curl checks passed (including duplicate 409, ftp/missing-URL 422, malformed JSON 422, redirects and click counts), and after a full server restart links and click counts survived. Test rows were cleaned up and the dev server stopped. README includes the startup instructions."
